<worksheet xml:id="ws-product-rule">
  <title>Product Rule Worksheet</title>

  <objectives>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          State the product rule for differentiating a product of two functions.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <p>
          Apply the product rule to compute derivatives of products involving polynomials, trigonometric, and exponential functions.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <p>
          Recognize when the product rule is needed, and when it is not.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <page>

    <p>
      When a function is built by multiplying two simpler functions, we cannot just multiply their derivatives. The <term>product rule</term> tells us what to do instead.
    </p>

    <definition xml:id="def-product-rule">
      <statement>
        <p>
          If <m>f</m> and <m>g</m> are differentiable functions, then
          <me>
            \frac{d}{dx}\bigl[f(x)\,g(x)\bigr]
            = f'(x)\,g(x) + f(x)\,g'(x).
          </me>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </definition>

    <p>
      Let's work through an example.
    </p>

    <example xml:id="ex-applying-product-rule">
      <title>Applying the product rule</title>

      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the derivative of <m>h(x) = x^2 \sin(x)</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <solution>
        <p>
          Let <m>f = x^2</m> and <m>g = \sin(x)</m>, so <m>f' = 2x</m> and <m>g' = \cos(x)</m>. By <xref ref="def-product-rule"/>,
          <me>
            h'(x) = f'(x)\,g(x) + f(x)\,g'(x)
                  = 2x\sin(x) + x^2 \cos(x).
          </me>
        </p>
      </solution>
    </example>

    <exercise workspace="2.5in">
      <title>Practice</title>

      <introduction>
        <p>
          Use the product rule (<xref ref="def-product-rule"/>) to find the derivative of each function.
        </p>
      </introduction>

      <task>
        <statement>
          <p>
            <m>p(x) = x^3 e^x</m>
          </p>
        </statement>
        <answer>
          <p>
            <m>p'(x) = 3x^2 e^x + x^3 e^x</m>.
          </p>
        </answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement>
          <p>
            <m>q(x) = (2x + 1)\cos(x)</m>
          </p>
        </statement>
        <answer>
          <p>
            <m>q'(x) = 2\cos(x) - (2x+1)\sin(x)</m>.
          </p>
        </answer>
      </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>

</worksheet>